WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.877
-I'm Jannis Niewöhner.
-And I'm George MacKay.

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.338
We're from the cast of
Munich - The Edge of War.

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:07.049
And we're going to attempt
to answer questions,

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:08.884
whilst playing Jenga.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.346
-Keep it cool man.
-Pals.

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:13.972
Let me start with this one
down here.

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:16.767
Careful.

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:20.395
30th September?

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:23.357
You went specific. 1938?

00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:27.027
One week to shoot a scene.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.488
The whole scene was
supposed to be in English,

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:31.907
but then it was supposed
to be in German.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.408
You had one week
to learn all the lines,

00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:35.077
so it's definitely George.

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:40.249
-Already?
-I know what you mean.

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:43.836
-I think the Brow house one?
-Absolutely, yeah.

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:45.629
We had to improvise a bit,
right?

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.631
Bring our own arguments
to the scene,

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.092
to the discussion
and that was really--

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:51.677
I was scared of that.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.136
The people of a whole county

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.055
forgot about
what makes them as a nation

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.182
and now that there is
someone to lead them

00:00:57.266 --> 00:01:00.227
and to remind them
of their nation's greatness.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:02.062
I had to keep it cool,
like now

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:02.980
Yeah.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.273
It was just like this.

00:01:04.356 --> 00:01:05.983
We were playing Jenga
but it got edited out.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.192
Fucking hell.

00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:08.527
We'll leave that there.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:09.736
We're both pretty good
in the morning.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.446
I love an early morning sun.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.614
I'm gonna say Jannis,

00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:13.824
just 'cause I really like
early mornings.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.200
It's definitely George.

00:01:15.284 --> 00:01:17.744
It's making it wobble.

00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:19.538
I think maybe the argument
in the car.

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:20.706
There's other ways
of doing thing.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:21.915
There's talk,
there's discussion

00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:23.417
There's no other things. No!

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.543
There's always hope.

00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:26.628
You know, we did that again,
and again, and again.

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:28.672
That we were sort
of speaking

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.090
and kind of get to
log ahead.

00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:34.428
The big, amazing hotel
in Dresden

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:35.971
Yeah, that was great.

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:37.556
Which kind of,
doubled as the area

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:39.683
before the meeting
took place.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.310
The place were,
all the kind of,

00:01:41.393 --> 00:01:42.686
political parties
were staying.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.354
That was an amazing hotel
in Dresden.

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:45.856
Dresden was an amazing city.

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:50.027
It is!

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.612
It is now.

00:01:51.695 --> 00:01:53.071
We got it!

00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:55.282
Should I take this out
really fast?

00:01:55.908 --> 00:01:57.326
-Yeah.
-I think I can do it.

00:01:58.577 --> 00:02:00.454
Cut, cut, cut.
Let me do it again.

00:02:01.538 --> 00:02:02.497
Magic.

00:02:03.207 --> 00:02:04.917
Munich - The Edge of War
is now streaming.

